---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="How I Work — AraGrow LLC"
  description="How David Aragó engages with clients: the first 90 days, engagement structure, tiers, and what to expect. Fractional CTO for businesses between $5M and $10M."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="hw-page">

    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="hw-header">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-label">Process</div>
        <h1 class="hw-title">Working with AraGrow</h1>
        <p class="hw-intro">
          Senior technology leadership plus hands-on execution, without the cost or overhead of a full-time CTO.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="container hw-container">

      <!-- What I Do -->
      <section class="hw-section">
        <h2 class="hw-section-title">What I Do</h2>
        <div class="hw-prose">
          <p>
            I help growing companies that have outgrown their current technology figure out what is actually
            slowing them down, fix the right problems first, and make better technology decisions without the
            cost or overhead of a full-time CTO.
          </p>
          <p>
            This is not strategy from the sidelines. It is senior technology leadership plus hands-on execution:
            audits, roadmaps, system cleanup, vendor evaluation, migrations, integrations, and practical
            decision-making inside the tools your team already uses.
          </p>
          <p>
            My best fit is a company in the $5M to $10M range that has grown to the point where technology is
            starting to create drag. Systems do not connect cleanly, too much knowledge lives in a few people,
            important work still depends on manual steps, and leadership needs a clearer view of what to fix
            now versus later.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- What Clients Get -->
      <section class="hw-section">
        <h2 class="hw-section-title">What Clients Get</h2>
        <p class="hw-section-note">Every engagement is built around clarity, momentum, and practical follow-through.</p>
        <ul class="hw-gets">
          <li>A clear view of the current technology environment, including weak points, workarounds, and single points of failure.</li>
          <li>A practical roadmap that helps the business decide what to fix, what to defer, and what to stop doing.</li>
          <li>Hands-on support inside the systems that matter, whether that means CRM, cloud tools, analytics, websites, codebases, or vendor evaluation.</li>
          <li>Regular communication that keeps decisions moving without forcing everything into meetings.</li>
          <li>Written updates in plain language so leadership understands what changed, what matters, and what needs attention next.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- How I Work -->
      <section class="hw-section">
        <h2 class="hw-section-title">How I Work</h2>
        <div class="hw-structure-grid">
          <div class="hw-structure-item">
            <div class="hw-structure-icon" aria-hidden="true">📅</div>
            <div>
              <strong>Weekly working session</strong>
              <p>Review priorities, make decisions, and remove blockers.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="hw-structure-item">
            <div class="hw-structure-icon" aria-hidden="true">💬</div>
            <div>
              <strong>Shared communication channel</strong>
              <p>Slack or email for questions between meetings. No waiting until the next session.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="hw-structure-item">
            <div class="hw-structure-icon" aria-hidden="true">🔧</div>
            <div>
              <strong>Hands-on time in your tools</strong>
              <p>CRM, cloud console, analytics, codebase — wherever the work actually lives.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="hw-structure-item">
            <div class="hw-structure-icon" aria-hidden="true">📄</div>
            <div>
              <strong>Monthly written summary</strong>
              <p>Progress, next steps, and key risks in plain language. Not a technical report.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="hw-structure-note">
          I do not disappear after a strategy document. I stay involved in the work, help the team move forward,
          and keep attention on the decisions that matter most.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- First 90 Days -->
      <section class="hw-section">
        <h2 class="hw-section-title">The First 90 Days</h2>
        <p class="hw-section-note">The first three months follow a consistent pattern.</p>
        <div class="hw-timeline">
          <div class="hw-phase">
            <div class="hw-phase-label">Weeks 1–2</div>
            <div class="hw-phase-content">
              <h3 class="hw-phase-title">Technology Audit</h3>
              <p>A current-state review of the systems you use, how they connect, where the business is exposed, and what is creating friction. This is where hidden dependencies, outdated assumptions, and operational drag start to become visible.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="hw-phase">
            <div class="hw-phase-label">Weeks 3–4</div>
            <div class="hw-phase-content">
              <h3 class="hw-phase-title">Stakeholder Conversations</h3>
              <p>Conversations with leadership and the people closest to the work to understand where the business needs to go over the next 12 to 18 months and where technology is helping or getting in the way.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="hw-phase">
            <div class="hw-phase-label">Month 2</div>
            <div class="hw-phase-content">
              <h3 class="hw-phase-title">Priority Roadmap</h3>
              <p>A clear written plan for what to fix first, what can wait, and what should stop. Not a large theoretical document. A practical guide the team can use.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="hw-phase">
            <div class="hw-phase-label">Month 3</div>
            <div class="hw-phase-content">
              <h3 class="hw-phase-title">First Implementation</h3>
              <p>One meaningful change that proves progress early. That may be an integration fix, a process improvement, a vendor decision, a reporting improvement, or another high-value change that reduces friction and builds confidence.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Engagement Options -->
      <section class="hw-section">
        <h2 class="hw-section-title">Engagement Options</h2>
        <div class="hw-tiers">
          <div class="hw-tier">
            <div class="hw-tier-name">Technology Clarity</div>
            <p class="hw-tier-for">For companies that need a senior technology sounding board and clearer direction.</p>
            <ul class="hw-tier-includes">
              <li>Advisory sessions</li>
              <li>Async support</li>
              <li>Written summaries</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="hw-tier-price">Custom scope — <a href="/contact">ask about fit</a></p>
          </div>
          <div class="hw-tier hw-tier-featured">
            <div class="hw-tier-badge">Most common</div>
            <div class="hw-tier-name">Technology in Motion</div>
            <p class="hw-tier-for">For companies actively building, migrating, fixing, or integrating something important.</p>
            <ul class="hw-tier-includes">
              <li>Weekly sessions</li>
              <li>Hands-on work</li>
              <li>Team coordination</li>
              <li>Monthly summaries</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="hw-tier-price">$1,500–$3,000/month <span>· 10–20 hours · $150/hr</span></p>
          </div>
          <div class="hw-tier">
            <div class="hw-tier-name">Technology Reset</div>
            <p class="hw-tier-for">For companies facing a major decision, transition, migration, or rebuild.</p>
            <ul class="hw-tier-includes">
              <li>Full first-90-days engagement</li>
              <li>Roadmap</li>
              <li>Vendor evaluation</li>
              <li>Architecture support</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="hw-tier-price">Starts with the 30-day audit <span>· up to $3,000</span></p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="hw-rate">
          No tiers, no minimums, no surprises. Billed at $150/hour — most clients land between $1,500 and $3,000/month.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Working Principles -->
      <section class="hw-section">
        <h2 class="hw-section-title">Working Principles</h2>
        <ul class="hw-principles">
          <li>Stay close to the work, not just the strategy.</li>
          <li>Reduce dependency instead of creating it.</li>
          <li>Choose the simplest solution that solves the real problem.</li>
          <li>Keep communication direct, useful, and understandable.</li>
          <li>Limit active clients so each engagement gets proper attention.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Based in Minnesota -->
      <section class="hw-section hw-section-location">
        <h2 class="hw-section-title">Based in Minnesota</h2>
        <p>
          AraGrow LLC is based in Minnesota and works with US clients through that Minnesota business structure.
          I spend part of the year in Spain, but the work model is already built for reliable remote
          collaboration, clear communication, and steady execution.
        </p>
        <p>
          Engagements are designed to be async-friendly. Written updates handle routine communication, while
          meetings are used for decisions, alignment, and problem-solving. This keeps projects moving without
          creating unnecessary meeting overhead.
        </p>
        <p>I work professionally in both English and Spanish.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- CTA -->
      <section class="hw-cta-block">
        <h2 class="hw-cta-title">Ready to talk?</h2>
        <p class="hw-cta-body">
          The best first step is a 30-minute conversation about where your technology is creating friction,
          what is changing in the business, and whether I am the right fit to help.
        </p>
        <div class="hw-cta-actions">
          <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Book a 30-minute conversation →</a>
          <a href="/self-assessment" class="hw-cta-secondary">Take the free self-assessment first</a>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  /* ── Header ── */
  .hw-header {
    background: linear-gradient(160deg, #5a1010 0%, #4a0c0c 55%, #3b0a0a 100%);
    color: #fdf6f4;
    padding: 80px 0 60px;
  }
  .hw-header .section-label { color: #E8B931; }
  .hw-title {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.1;
    color: #fdf6f4; margin: 12px 0 20px;
  }
  .hw-intro {
    font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7;
    color: rgba(253,246,244,0.8);
    max-width: 600px;
  }

  /* ── Container ── */
  .hw-container { padding-top: 56px; padding-bottom: 80px; }

  /* ── Sections ── */
  .hw-section {
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    padding: 40px;
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 16px;
  }
  .hw-section-title {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--teal-text);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    padding-bottom: 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .hw-section-note {
    font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 24px; line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* ── Prose ── */
  .hw-prose p {
    font-size: 0.97rem; line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .hw-prose p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  /* ── What Clients Get ── */
  .hw-gets {
    list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px;
  }
  .hw-gets li {
    font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--muted);
    padding-left: 22px; position: relative;
  }
  .hw-gets li::before {
    content: '→';
    position: absolute; left: 0;
    color: var(--teal-text); font-size: 0.85rem;
    top: 2px;
  }

  /* ── Engagement structure ── */
  .hw-structure-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .hw-structure-item {
    display: flex; gap: 14px;
    padding: 18px;
    background: var(--dark);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
  }
  .hw-structure-icon { font-size: 1.3rem; flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 2px; }
  .hw-structure-item strong {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.93rem; font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 5px;
  }
  .hw-structure-item p {
    font-size: 0.87rem; line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--muted); margin: 0;
  }
  .hw-structure-note {
    font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--muted);
    padding: 14px 18px;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--teal-text);
    background: var(--teal-dim);
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
  }

  /* ── Timeline ── */
  .hw-timeline {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--border);
    margin-left: 12px;
  }
  .hw-phase {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 110px 1fr;
    gap: 20px;
    padding: 0 0 32px 28px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .hw-phase::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: -6px; top: 6px;
    width: 10px; height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--teal-text);
    border: 2px solid var(--card);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--teal-text);
  }
  .hw-phase:last-child { padding-bottom: 0; }
  .hw-phase-label {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--teal-text);
    text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    padding-top: 4px;
  }
  .hw-phase-title {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.97rem; font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .hw-phase-content p {
    font-size: 0.91rem; line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--muted); margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── Tiers ── */
  .hw-tiers {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .hw-tier {
    padding: 24px;
    background: var(--dark);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .hw-tier-featured {
    background: var(--card);
    border-color: var(--teal-text);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(123,24,24,0.1);
  }
  .hw-tier-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--teal-text);
    background: var(--teal-dim);
    padding: 3px 10px; border-radius: 999px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .hw-tier-name {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.97rem; font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .hw-tier-for {
    font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .hw-tier-includes {
    list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px;
  }
  .hw-tier-includes li {
    font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text);
    padding-left: 16px; position: relative;
  }
  .hw-tier-includes li::before {
    content: '·';
    position: absolute; left: 4px;
    color: var(--teal-text); font-weight: 700;
  }
  .hw-tier-price {
    margin-top: 16px;
    padding-top: 12px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 0.88rem; font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--teal-text);
  }
  .hw-tier-price span {
    font-weight: 400; color: var(--muted);
  }
  .hw-tier-price a {
    color: var(--teal-text); text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .hw-tier-price a:hover { color: var(--teal); }

  .hw-rate {
    font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  /* ── Working Principles ── */
  .hw-principles {
    list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px;
  }
  .hw-principles li {
    font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--muted);
    padding-left: 22px; position: relative;
  }
  .hw-principles li::before {
    content: '✓';
    position: absolute; left: 0;
    color: var(--teal-text);
    font-size: 0.8rem; top: 3px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  /* ── Location ── */
  .hw-section-location p {
    font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .hw-section-location p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  /* ── CTA block ── */
  .hw-cta-block {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 56px 24px;
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 16px;
  }
  .hw-cta-title {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .hw-cta-body {
    font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--muted); max-width: 520px;
    margin: 0 auto 28px;
  }
  .hw-cta-actions {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center; gap: 14px;
  }
  .hw-cta-secondary {
    font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--teal-text);
    text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .hw-cta-secondary:hover { color: var(--teal); }

  /* ── Responsive ── */
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .hw-tiers { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .hw-tier-featured { order: -1; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .hw-section { padding: 24px 20px; }
    .hw-structure-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .hw-phase { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; }
    .hw-phase-label { padding-top: 0; }
    .hw-cta-block { padding: 40px 20px; }
  }
</style>
